<strong class="text-strong">Work In Progress : Mk-race : A free blender game usign Bullets Physics</strong><br><br>Hi  everybody,<br><br>I am Monster_kill and I'm working on a project with my team.<br>It's a car game where you are in a new galaxy. The human race has discovered it, and they found that it's controlled by ROBOTS.<br>A competition in this galaxy has been launched. Start your "game'life" here. Take a car (or more  <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_mrgreen.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":mrgreen:" title="Mr. Green"> ) and win the price for each planet !!!<br><br>Actually the galaxy has not been created, so please Wait  <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"><br><br>The official website of the future game is here : <a href="http://mk-race.fr.nf" class="postlink">Mk-race website (French only)</a><br><br>The game is created with Blender and it use the Physics Bullet Library. Erwin Coumans give me the authorization to use  <a href="http://mk-race.fr.nf/vehicle" class="postlink">this script</a>. And i have customed this script for cars in the game.<br><br>I will give you updates if there are.<br>@+<br>Monster_kill<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2357">Monster_kill</a> — Mon Mar 31, 2008 12:26 pm</p><hr />
